{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observed problem\n`infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` configures `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors` with `evaluation_periods = 6`, `datapoints_to_alarm = 3`, and `period = 300`. Its `alarm_description` still says it pages on \"3 of 5 five-minute periods.\" That text is sent to CloudWatch/SNS and contradicts the deployed threshold.\n\n## Verification (2026-10-24)\n- Live alarm `rebar-gerrit-voter-errors` (us-east-1): EvaluationPeriods 6, DatapointsToAlarm 3, Period 300, TreatMissingData notBreaching; its live description says \"3 of 5 five-minute\" (874 characters).\n- The tuning runbook (`infra/runbooks/alarm-window-tuning.md`) already records this alarm as `300/6/3`, so the description is the stale side.\n- Survey of all 43 alarm blocks: only 2 descriptions contain an \"N of M\" claim, and only `voter_errors` disagrees with its HCL (`review_interrupts_signal_unavailable` says 2 of 4 and is 2 of 4).\n- Longest effective description (after the `<<-` heredoc strips indentation) is 1,021 characters against CloudWatch's 1,024 limit; the edited voter description keeps its length.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf`, change \"3 of 5 five-minute periods\" to \"3 of 6 five-minute periods\" in the description. Leave the \"~15 minutes\" claim: 3 consecutive 5-minute breaching buckets of a stuck voter are still 15 minutes.\n2. In `tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py`, parse each alarm's description and fail when an \"N of M\" (or \"N-of-M\") window claim differs from `datapoints_to_alarm` of `evaluation_periods`. Seed the check with a mismatched example that must be flagged and a matching one that must pass, and keep a floor on the number of claims found so the parser cannot go blind. The 1,024 limit is already enforced by `tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py` (in bytes, the provider's unit), so no second length check is added.\n3. Change no thresholds, dimensions, actions or missing-data behaviour.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` and `tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py`. Out of scope: applying Terraform to the live alarm (an operator step) and the other alarms' wording.\n\n## Testing\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py -q\npytest tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py -q\nterraform fmt -check infra/terraform\nmake verify\n```\nFailure case: before the HCL edit the new drift test fails naming `voter_errors`; the seeded mismatched description must be flagged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The `voter_errors` description in the HCL says 3 of 6 five-minute periods and matches `datapoints_to_alarm` and `evaluation_periods` (checked: new test passes after the edit and fails before it).\n- [x] The drift test covers every alarm and rejects a seeded mismatched description (checked: seeded test).\n- [x] The edited description still fits the provider limit (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py -q` passes).\n- [x] `make verify` is green on the Linux CI gate (`Verified +1` on the Gerrit change).\n\n## Follow-up\nThe live CloudWatch description changes only when an operator applies Terraform; that apply is tracked in its own ticket rather than held open here.\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792841685863044001,"uuid":"341e96f9-32d4-4118-b27c-15bdc98f6b10"}